# examples/games/06_tetris, played: a line cleared and a best score kept,
# then a game lost.
#
# Seed 1 deals T I J Z S L O, then L O J S T Z I, from a 7-bag; a piece
# appears at column 5 and falls a row every half second, or every 3 frames
# while KEY_DOWN is held. KEY_LEFT and KEY_RIGHT move it one column per press
# and KEY_ENTER turns it a quarter, each one press = one step -- so a key
# tapped again has to come up for a frame in between. The save folder starts
# empty every run (tests/e2e/driver.cpp), so the best score starts at 0.
# See tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar.

# --- the happy path: a line ---------------------------------------------------

# T: turned twice, flat side down, and dropped where it is: columns 4-6.
1 tap KEY_ENTER
3 tap KEY_ENTER
4 shot t_turned_twice
4 press KEY_DOWN
64 release KEY_DOWN

# I: four to the left, columns 0-3.
65 tap KEY_LEFT
67 tap KEY_LEFT
69 tap KEY_LEFT
71 tap KEY_LEFT
72 press KEY_DOWN
131 release KEY_DOWN

# J: three to the right, columns 7-9 -- and the bottom row is full.
132 tap KEY_RIGHT
134 tap KEY_RIGHT
136 tap KEY_RIGHT
137 press KEY_DOWN
193 shot line_cleared
193 expect scene TetrisScene

# --- the failure path: the well fills up -------------------------------------

# Everything else straight down the middle, until a piece has no room to
# appear. One line beats a best of 0: "New best!", and it is saved.
461 expect scene TetrisScene
462 expect scene OverScene
463 release KEY_DOWN
470 shot new_best

# Play again, from the keyboard: the one button has the focus. The new game
# reads the best score back from the save.
472 tap KEY_ENTER
472 expect scene TetrisScene
474 shot best_read_back
474 press KEY_DOWN

# And straight down the middle again, with no line this time: the best score
# stands, and the game says so.
793 expect scene TetrisScene
794 expect scene OverScene
800 shot game_over
800 end
